It does not use "int" and such as keywords, but as classes.

In C, int, bool, char etc. are primitive data types.
In C#, int, bool, char etc. are aliases for System.Int32, System.Boolean, System.Char. These types are part of the .NET Framework and are defined in the System namespace. In fact, you can use either C# aliases or the full type name in .NET. For example:

int i = 123;
System.Int32 i2 = 123;

